				<r3d:description language="eng">As a department of the United States Department of Agriculture (USDA) the National Agricultural Statistics Service (NASS) continually surveys and reports on U.S. agriculture.  NASS reports include production and supplies of food and fiber, prices paid and received by farmers, farm labor and wages, farm finances, chemical use, and changes in the demographics of U.S. producers.  NASS provides objective and unbiased statistics of states and counties, while safeguarding the privacy of farmers and ranchers.</r3d:description>
